window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-4f9f8c3f852c1911"]={"key":"ny_b1-4f9f8c3f852c1911","group":"ny_b1","uid":"4f9f8c3f852c1911","rank":74,"title":"cassilis principal preference profile blank instrument","occupation":"concierges","archetype":"artifact_spec","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Nnamdi Falkenrath, a concierge at Cassilis House Management, and Ingrid Solheim, our principal-services director, has asked for a dependable intake workbook before she reviews the first Wintergate Engineering family-office batch on 30 September. We currently keep one master clienteling sheet for all principals, but it was written as shorthand for people who already knew the households rather than as a record that can be handed to a new concierge or checked by an external client. The source workbook is `cassilis_master_clienteling.xlsx`; use it to understand the kind of notes we have today, including entries associated with Ivo Chakraborty, Maude Oyelaran, Elena Reinholt, Henrik Lindqvist, and Zeynep Gasparyan. Wintergate Engineering has supplied the fixed intake schema in `wintergate_preference_schema.xlsx`, and that schema is the authority for the field names, required indicators, permitted values, and the order in which the client's reviewers expect the profile to be read. Please also use the handling guidance in `northgale_data_handling_note.docx`, which was prepared for the Northgale Clinic liaison process and sets out the distinction between an explicit source statement, a safe normalization, a follow-up item, and an unsupported assumption, as well as the review brief in `principal_services_review_brief.docx`, which explains how the finished profile will be checked and printed. Create a blank, reusable per-principal preference profile template in `principal_preference_profile.xlsx` and place that file at the top level of the working directory, using exactly that filename. It must cover the client's complete schema exactly rather than quietly dropping fields that are inconvenient to source; in particular, dietary escalation contact, allergy severity tier, and standing car preference need to be visible even when the current master sheet does not support a value. Include a source-mapping key in the same workbook so the next concierge can see the master-sheet field or note pattern that may populate each client field, the allowed normalization where one is justified, what evidence is required, and when the field must remain blank and be referred for confirmation. The mapping key is a working control, not a second place to invent a profile, so do not populate the profile with examples from the master sheet and do not copy any principal's personal values into the blank template. Keep source wording and client wording distinguishable, preserve provenance, and make unsupported gaps obvious without turning them into guessed “not applicable” answers. The workbook will be completed on screen and then printed for Ingrid's review and occasionally sent as a controlled attachment to the client's principal-services team, so a new concierge should be able to tell where to enter a value, which choices are controlled, which fields are required, and what an unresolved gap means without a verbal handover. Use the exact headings, field labels, controlled vocabulary, and escalation terminology supplied in the referenced files rather than inventing local synonyms. Make the profile convenient to scan, but do not merge or visually abbreviate fields in a way that changes the client's schema or obscures the distinction between a blank, a confirmed preference, and a follow-up. The workbook must continue to work when additional principals and additional master-sheet rows are added later; do not build formulas, named ranges, validation lists, or completeness checks around only the rows visible today. Where a completion indicator or summary is useful, it must be formula-driven and must not claim that a profile is complete merely because cells contain placeholders. Keep all profile-entry cells genuinely empty at delivery, including optional fields and unresolved fields; labels, instructions, mapping rules, validation controls, and formulas that explain the blank instrument are fine, but sample answers are not. Set up the workbook so the fields that require controlled responses use the client's permitted choices, and make missing required information visually apparent without changing the underlying value or filling it automatically. Set up printing so the profile is legible on A4 paper at the review desk, with the profile readable without clipped columns and the source-mapping material usable as a separate reference page. Do not add a logo, invented client data, live links, macros, passwords, or a second deliverable. Before returning it, open the workbook and inspect the formulas, validations, conditional formatting, defined names, expansion behaviour, and print settings rather than relying only on how the first screen looks.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/cassilis_master_clienteling.xlsx` — The current shorthand master clienteling workbook. It contains complete, internally consistent source notes and field values for the named principals and is the source material from which legitimate mappings must be identified.\n- `references/wintergate_preference_schema.xlsx` — Wintergate Engineering's mandated principal preference schema, including exact field labels, required status, controlled vocabularies, field order, and client-facing terminology.\n- `references/northgale_data_handling_note.docx` — Operational guidance defining explicit evidence, safe normalization, follow-up status, unsupported inference, and escalation treatment for sensitive or absent preference information.\n- `references/principal_services_review_brief.docx` — The principal-services director's review and print requirements, including how the blank template, completion indication, mapping key, and unresolved items will be used.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `principal_preference_profile.xlsx` — A blank per-principal preference profile workbook containing the exact Wintergate schema and a source-mapping key. (Write the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.; Keep every profile-entry cell empty at delivery; do not include examples, copied principal values, guessed values, or placeholder answers.; Use the exact field labels, controlled values, escalation terms, and required indicators from the supplied schema and handling guidance.; Make formulas, named ranges, validations, conditional formatting, and print settings continue to function when source data grows beyond the supplied rows.; The mapping key must document source evidence, permitted normalization, provenance expectations, and deliberate-blank or follow-up treatment for every client field.; The workbook must open without repair warnings and must not contain macros, external links, logos, or passwords.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/cassilis_master_clienteling.xlsx","bytes":7197,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/2b42d9917ec85ca30aa9ce68d85a09212907d5f2b2fba3e60bf70b79d0f21aea.xlsx","sha256":"2b42d9917ec85ca30aa9ce68d85a09212907d5f2b2fba3e60bf70b79d0f21aea","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Clienteling Export","row_count":8,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Cassilis House Management — Clienteling master"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Principal notes export | 16 Sep 2026 18:40 | internal working copy"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Client_Code","Principal Name","Preferred address","Dietary note","Allergies / handling","Beverage notes","Room note","Arrival preference","Privacy preference","Contact pathway","Transport notes","Travel remarks","Last touch"]},{"r":"5","cells":["CHM-0184","Ivo Chakraborty","Dr.","Vegetarian; no red meat","Shellfish allergy — severity not recorded","Still water, Assam tea","","Lobby meet","Enhanced confidentiality","Assistant","Airport transfer booked: executive sedan, 14 Sep","Prefers early check-in when travelling from Singapore","2026-09-14"]},{"r":"6","cells":["CHM-0221","Maude Oyelaran","First name preferred","Avoid pork","Kiwi allergy; no reaction detail","Mint tea after meetings","","Curbside meet","Standard","Email","","","2026-09-11"]},{"r":"7","cells":["CHM-0306","Elena Reinholt","Ms","","","Sparkling water","Always cool room; avoid fragrance","Discreet arrival","Principal approval required","Secure portal","","Rail preferred for European city pairs","2026-09-08"]},{"r":"8","cells":["CHM-0377","Henrik Lindqvist","Mr","","","Espresso; sparkling water","","","Standard","Telephone","One-off transfer: electric sedan for Copenhagen station","","2026-09-15"]},{"r":"9","cells":["CHM-0419","Zeynep Gasparyan","Dr","Halal meals requested","Tree-nut allergy — confirmation requested","","Warmer room in winter","Lobby meet","Enhanced confidentiality","Assistant","Airport run completed in SUV","Avoid connections under 55 minutes","2026-09-16"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/northgale_data_handling_note.docx","bytes":37451,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/8409e70ca8f72a376798556120730481b1c2d77d72f257ad1f818c45918dc636.docx","sha256":"8409e70ca8f72a376798556120730481b1c2d77d72f257ad1f818c45918dc636","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Northgale Clinic liaison process\nData handling note — preference evidence and escalation\nUse this control when transferring concise liaison notes into a client-facing preference record. It applies to sensitive information and ordinary service preferences alike.\nExplicit source statement\nA source may populate a profile only where it states the relevant preference, restriction, authorised contact, or instruction directly for the same person. Absence is not evidence of no preference.\nSafe normalization\nA safe normalization changes presentation, not meaning: capitalization, punctuation, or a stated synonym to the client’s controlled choice. Record both the source wording and the normalized client wording. Do not convert a one-off instruction into a standing preference.\nFollow-up item\nWhere wording is incomplete, ambiguous, or not on the client list, leave the destination field blank and create a follow-up item for confirmation. A blank is not a negative answer and must not be replaced by “N/A,” “none,” or an assumed default.\nUnsupported assumption\nDo not infer allergy severity from an allergen, an escalation contact from a household role, or a standing car from a booked journey. These need explicit evidence. Sensitive or safety-related gaps are referred to Principal Services for confirmation.\nProvenance\nFor every populated field retain the master row or original note, source wording, any safe normalization, date checked, and reviewer. Do not overwrite the source wording with the client-facing wording.\nPrepared for liaison operations | Version 2.1 | 07 September 2026","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/principal_services_review_brief.docx","bytes":37407,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/c8168fdf1843653c9f0538123c1fc47a443fb255e95ab1a8afd255fadcd5803c.docx","sha256":"c8168fdf1843653c9f0538123c1fc47a443fb255e95ab1a8afd255fadcd5803c","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Principal Services review brief\nFor Ingrid Solheim — Wintergate Engineering family-office intake\nThe intake workbook will be completed electronically by a concierge before the 30 September review. It must be understandable to a new team member without a verbal handover and may be printed for desk review or sent as a controlled attachment to the client team.\nProfile\nUse the Wintergate field order and client terminology. Keep every destination value distinct from its source wording. Required fields need a visible unresolved signal until an actual answer is entered; no placeholder may satisfy the completion indicator.\nControlled entry\nChoices supplied by Wintergate must be selected from their approved vocabulary. Free-text fields must remain empty until supported evidence is available.\nMapping reference\nProvide a separate operational mapping key for every profile field. It must show the source relationship, evidence threshold, safe normalization, blank or confirmation path, and provenance to retain.\nPrint and review\nSet the Profile for A4 portrait and one page wide. Set the mapping reference for A4 landscape, one page wide, with its header repeated on subsequent pages. Keep useful headers visible while staff scroll.\nGrowth\nThe template is reusable. Do not tie controls, formulas, mapping ranges, or validation lists to the current number of master records.\nPrincipal Services | Internal review brief | 15 September 2026","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/wintergate_preference_schema.xlsx","bytes":7503,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/7a76692a36adbc14e1fff9135b3103e56e946ae7f6af6efaeef5e9c1a838129a.xlsx","sha256":"7a76692a36adbc14e1fff9135b3103e56e946ae7f6af6efaeef5e9c1a838129a","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Wintergate schema","row_count":52,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Wintergate Engineering — Principal preference profile intake schema"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Issued 12 September 2026 | Client review order is fixed"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Field label","Required indicator","Field type","Permitted values"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Principal full name","Required","Free text",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["Principal reference ID","Required","Free text",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Preferred form of address","Required","Controlled list","Form of address"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Dietary preferences","Optional","Free text",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Dietary escalation contact","Required","Free text",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["Allergy details","Required","Free text",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["Allergy severity tier","Required","Controlled list","Allergy severity tier"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Beverage preferences","Optional","Free text",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["Room environment","Optional","Controlled list","Room environment"]},{"r":"14","cells":["Standing car preference","Required","Controlled list","Standing car preference"]},{"r":"15","cells":["Arrival assistance","Required","Controlled list","Arrival assistance"]},{"r":"16","cells":["Privacy handling","Required","Controlled list","Privacy handling"]},{"r":"17","cells":["Communication channel","Required","Controlled list","Communication channel"]},{"r":"18","cells":["Travel notes","Optional","Free text",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["Review escalation status","Required","Controlled list","Review escalation status"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Controlled vocabulary","","",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["Field label","Permitted value","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["Form of address","Ms"]},{"r":"26","cells":["Form of address","Mr"]},{"r":"27","cells":["Form of address","Dr"]},{"r":"28","cells":["Form of address","Mx"]},{"r":"29","cells":["Form of address","First name"]},{"r":"30","cells":["Allergy severity tier","Mild"]},{"r":"31","cells":["Allergy severity tier","Moderate"]},{"r":"32","cells":["Allergy severity tier","Severe"]},{"r":"33","cells":["Allergy severity tier","Anaphylaxis risk"]},{"r":"34","cells":["Room environment","Cooler"]},{"r":"35","cells":["Room environment","Neutral"]},{"r":"36","cells":["Room environment","Warmer"]},{"r":"37","cells":["Standing car preference","Executive sedan"]},{"r":"38","cells":["Standing car preference","SUV"]},{"r":"39","cells":["Standing car preference","Electric sedan"]},{"r":"40","cells":["Standing car preference","People carrier"]},{"r":"41","cells":["Standing car preference","No standing preference"]},{"r":"42","cells":["Arrival assistance","Curbside meet"]},{"r":"43","cells":["Arrival assistance","Lobby meet"]},{"r":"44","cells":["Arrival assistance","Discreet arrival"]},{"r":"45","cells":["Arrival assistance","No assistance requested"]},{"r":"46","cells":["Privacy handling","Standard"]},{"r":"47","cells":["Privacy handling","Enhanced confidentiality"]},{"r":"48","cells":["Privacy handling","Principal approval required"]},{"r":"49","cells":["Communication channel","Email"]},{"r":"50","cells":["Communication channel","Telephone"]},{"r":"51","cells":["Communication channel","Secure portal"]},{"r":"52","cells":["Communication channel","Assistant"]},{"r":"53","cells":["Review escalation status","No escalation required"]},{"r":"54","cells":["Review escalation status","Confirm with Principal Services"]},{"r":"55","cells":["Review escalation status","Confirm with authorised representative"]},{"r":"56","cells":["Review escalation status","Safety escalation required"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/principal_preference_profile.xlsx","bytes":14751,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/df350a7472cf943c8d7e13ff68404d7b361820d12aa1c29ce13ecb00f135d835.xlsx","sha256":"df350a7472cf943c8d7e13ff68404d7b361820d12aa1c29ce13ecb00f135d835","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Profile","row_count":21,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Wintergate Engineering — Principal Preference Profile"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Blank intake instrument | complete only from supported evidence | controlled attachment"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Required fields completed","=--(AND($B9=\"Required\",D9\u003c>\"\",D9\u003c>\"TBC\",D9\u003c>\"N/A\",D9\u003c>\"Unknown\",D9\u003c>\"-\"))+--(AND($B10=\"Required\",D10\u003c>\"\",D10\u003c>\"TBC\",D10\u003c>\"N/A\",D10\u003c>\"Unknown\",D10\u003c>\"-\"))+--(AND(AND($B11=\"Required\",D11\u003c>\"\",D11\u003c>\"TBC\",D11\u003c>\"N/A\",D11\u003c>\"Unknown\",D11\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D11,FormOfAddress,0))))+--(AND($B12=\"Required\",D12\u003c>\"\",D12\u003c>\"TBC\",D12\u003c>\"N/A\",D12\u003c>\"Unknown\",D12\u003c>\"-\"))+--(AND($B13=\"Required\",D13\u003c>\"\",D13\u003c>\"TBC\",D13\u003c>\"N/A\",D13\u003c>\"Unknown\",D13\u003c>\"-\"))+--(AND($B14=\"Required\",D14\u003c>\"\",D14\u003c>\"TBC\",D14\u003c>\"N/A\",D14\u003c>\"Unknown\",D14\u003c>\"-\"))+--(AND(AND($B15=\"Required\",D15\u003c>\"\",D15\u003c>\"TBC\",D15\u003c>\"N/A\",D15\u003c>\"Unknown\",D15\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D15,AllergySeverityTier,0))))+--(AND($B16=\"Required\",D16\u003c>\"\",D16\u003c>\"TBC\",D16\u003c>\"N/A\",D16\u003c>\"Unknown\",D16\u003c>\"-\"))+--(AND(AND($B17=\"Required\",D17\u003c>\"\",D17\u003c>\"TBC\",D17\u003c>\"N/A\",D17\u003c>\"Unknown\",D17\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D17,RoomEnvironment,0))))+--(AND(AND($B18=\"Required\",D18\u003c>\"\",D18\u003c>\"TBC\",D18\u003c>\"N/A\",D18\u003c>\"Unknown\",D18\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D18,StandingCarPreference,0))))+--(AND(AND($B19=\"Required\",D19\u003c>\"\",D19\u003c>\"TBC\",D19\u003c>\"N/A\",D19\u003c>\"Unknown\",D19\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D19,ArrivalAssistance,0))))+--(AND(AND($B20=\"Required\",D20\u003c>\"\",D20\u003c>\"TBC\",D20\u003c>\"N/A\",D20\u003c>\"Unknown\",D20\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D20,PrivacyHandling,0))))+--(AND(AND($B21=\"Required\",D21\u003c>\"\",D21\u003c>\"TBC\",D21\u003c>\"N/A\",D21\u003c>\"Unknown\",D21\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D21,CommunicationChannel,0))))+--(AND($B22=\"Required\",D22\u003c>\"\",D22\u003c>\"TBC\",D22\u003c>\"N/A\",D22\u003c>\"Unknown\",D22\u003c>\"-\"))+--(AND(AND($B23=\"Required\",D23\u003c>\"\",D23\u003c>\"TBC\",D23\u003c>\"N/A\",D23\u003c>\"Unknown\",D23\u003c>\"-\"),ISNUMBER(MATCH(D23,ReviewEscalationStatus,0))))  [缓存: 缺失]","","Entry cells are pale blue. Use the dropdown where present; record source-specific provenance beside each value."]},{"r":"5","cells":["Required fields total","=COUNTIF(ProfileFields[Required status],\"Required\")  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Review status","=IF(B4=B5,\"READY FOR REVIEW\",\"UNRESOLVED REQUIRED FIELDS\")  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Client field","Required status","Field type","Profile entry","Provenance record"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Principal full name","Required","Free text","",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["Principal reference ID","Required","Free text","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["Preferred form of address","Required","Controlled list","",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["Dietary preferences","Optional","Free text","",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["Dietary escalation contact","Required","Free text","",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["Allergy details","Required","Free text","",""]},{"r":"15","cells":["Allergy severity tier","Required","Controlled list","",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["Beverage preferences","Optional","Free text","",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["Room environment","Optional","Controlled list","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["Standing car preference","Required","Controlled list","",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["Arrival assistance","Required","Controlled list","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["Privacy handling","Required","Controlled list","",""]},{"r":"21","cells":["Communication channel","Required","Controlled list","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["Travel notes","Optional","Free text","",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["Review escalation status","Required","Controlled list","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Mapping Key","row_count":18,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Source-mapping key — Wintergate preference profile"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Working control: preserve source wording and provenance; do not use this sheet to invent a profile value."]},{"r":"4","cells":["Client field","Required status","Source field or note pattern","Evidence rule","Permitted normalization","If unsupported or absent","Provenance to retain"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Principal full name","Required","Principal Name","Use only an explicit source statement identifying the principal; do not derive a name from initials or another household record.","Copy exactly; retain the source spelling.","Leave blank and create a follow-up item for confirmation.","Record master row, source column, and review date."]},{"r":"6","cells":["Principal reference ID","Required","Client_Code","Use only the explicit identifier in Client_Code for the same principal record.","Copy exactly; do not create or shorten an identifier.","Leave blank and create a follow-up item for confirmation.","Record master row, Client_Code, and review date."]},{"r":"7","cells":["Preferred form of address","Required","Preferred address","An explicit address preference is required; initials or a name alone are not evidence.","Safe normalization: “Dr.” may be entered as “Dr”; otherwise select only the matching client choice.","Leave blank and refer for confirmation when the wording does not match a controlled choice.","Record master row, Preferred address wording, and reviewer."]},{"r":"8","cells":["Dietary preferences","Optional","Dietary note","Use an explicit dietary statement or restriction; absence is not “no preference.”","Copy the source wording or make only a safe punctuation/capitalization normalization.","Leave blank and create a follow-up item; do not enter “none” or “not applicable.”","Record master row, Dietary note wording, and date checked."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Dietary escalation contact","Required","No supported master field","This requires an explicit source statement naming or authorising an escalation contact.","No normalization is permitted without an explicit contact and authority.","Leave blank pending supported confirmation through Principal Services; record as a follow-up item.","Record confirmation source, authorised contact, date, and reviewer once confirmed."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Allergy details","Required","Allergies / handling","Use only an explicit allergy or handling statement; do not infer an allergy from a dietary choice.","Copy exact allergy wording; formatting-only normalization is safe.","Leave blank and refer for confirmation if the note is absent or ambiguous.","Record master row, Allergies / handling wording, and date checked."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Allergy severity tier","Required","Allergies / handling","A permitted severity tier must be explicitly stated. An allergy mention alone is not severity evidence.","Normalize only an explicitly stated equivalent of a client tier; never assign a tier from the allergen.","Leave blank and route as a follow-up item for confirmation when severity evidence is absent.","Record exact severity statement, source location, confirmation date, and reviewer."]},{"r":"12","cells":["Beverage preferences","Optional","Beverage notes","Use an explicit beverage preference; event catering instructions are not standing preferences.","Copy exact wording or apply punctuation/capitalization only.","Leave blank and create a follow-up item; do not assume from prior orders.","Record master row, Beverage notes wording, and date checked."]},{"r":"13","cells":["Room environment","Optional","Room note","Use an explicit room-temperature preference, not a temporary maintenance or weather comment.","Safe normalization: explicit “cool room” maps to “Cooler”; explicit “warm room” maps to “Warmer”.","Leave blank and refer for confirmation if no controlled choice is explicitly supported.","Record master row, Room note wording, normalized choice, and reviewer."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Standing car preference","Required","Transport notes","Use only an explicit standing, default, or always-use car preference. A one-off booking is not evidence.","Normalize only an explicit vehicle description to the matching controlled choice.","Leave blank and create a follow-up item when the source is a trip-specific transport note.","Record source wording, whether it states standing/default, date, and reviewer."]},{"r":"15","cells":["Arrival assistance","Required","Arrival preference","Use an explicit recurring arrival preference; a single event instruction requires confirmation.","Select the matching client choice; do not broaden “lobby” into another assistance type.","Leave blank and refer for confirmation when no recurring preference is explicit.","Record master row, Arrival preference wording, and reviewer."]},{"r":"16","cells":["Privacy handling","Required","Privacy preference","Use only an explicit privacy-handling instruction for the principal.","Select the matching client choice; no inference from seniority or travel pattern.","Leave blank and route for confirmation if the statement is absent or unclear.","Record master row, Privacy preference wording, and date checked."]},{"r":"17","cells":["Communication channel","Required","Contact pathway","Use only an explicit preferred channel or authorised intermediary.","Select the matching client choice; “assistant” is allowed only where the source explicitly identifies that pathway.","Leave blank and refer for confirmation if no channel is stated.","Record master row, Contact pathway wording, authority if applicable, and reviewer."]},{"r":"18","cells":["Travel notes","Optional","Travel remarks","Use explicit ongoing travel preferences; do not copy one-off itinerary logistics as a preference.","Copy exact wording or remove only redundant punctuation.","Leave blank and create a follow-up item when only an event-specific note exists.","Record master row, Travel remarks wording, and date checked."]},{"r":"19","cells":["Review escalation status","Required","No supported master field","This is set only after the current evidence review; it is not inferred from a blank source cell.","Select a client term that reflects the documented review path only.","Leave blank pending review; unresolved or sensitive gaps must be referred to Principal Services.","Record reviewer, review date, and linked confirmation or follow-up reference."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Instructions","row_count":8,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Using this blank profile"]},{"r":"2","cells":["For concierge completion and Ingrid Solheim review"]},{"r":"4","cells":["1. Enter supported values","Enter information only in the pale-blue Profile entry and Provenance record cells. Each row is one Wintergate field. Do not use a label, a placeholder, or a copied shorthand note as an answer."]},{"r":"5","cells":["2. Use controlled choices","Rows marked Controlled list have a dropdown in the Profile entry cell. Select only a Wintergate permitted choice. Free-text fields remain empty until supported evidence is available."]},{"r":"6","cells":["3. Read unresolved required fields","Pale-red highlighting means a Required field has no actual entry. The completion indicator counts required entries only when they are nonblank and not TBC, N/A, Unknown, or a dash. READY FOR REVIEW appears only when all required entries count."]},{"r":"7","cells":["4. Use the mapping key","For every field, use the Mapping Key to find the legitimate master field or note pattern, evidence threshold, permitted safe normalization, and the provenance to record. Preserve source wording in the provenance record when you enter client wording."]},{"r":"8","cells":["5. Escalate unsupported information","A blank value is not the same as no preference. When evidence is absent, ambiguous, sensitive, or only a one-off event, leave the Profile entry blank and create a follow-up item for confirmation through Principal Services or the authorised representative. Do not guess."]},{"r":"9","cells":["6. Review and print","Complete the profile on screen, review the completion indicator and provenance, then print the Profile on A4 portrait. Print the Mapping Key separately on A4 landscape when it is needed for the review handoff."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Lists","row_count":6,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Form of address","Allergy severity tier","Room environment","Standing car preference","Arrival assistance","Privacy handling","Communication channel","Review escalation status"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Ms","Mild","Cooler","Executive sedan","Curbside meet","Standard","Email","No escalation required"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Mr","Moderate","Neutral","SUV","Lobby meet","Enhanced confidentiality","Telephone","Confirm with Principal Services"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Dr","Severe","Warmer","Electric sedan","Discreet arrival","Principal approval required","Secure portal","Confirm with authorised representative"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Mx","Anaphylaxis risk","","People carrier","No assistance requested","","Assistant","Safety escalation required"]},{"r":"6","cells":["First name","","","No standing preference"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted workbook opens successfully as a valid XLSX without repair warnings, missing parts, or unreadable worksheets.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook opening and package inspection.","grader_hint":"Open with a spreadsheet library and inspect the OOXML package; reject if repair is required or any required sheet cannot be read."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains the three operational areas Profile, Mapping Key, and Instructions.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet names.","grader_hint":"Inspect workbook.sheetnames."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Profile area contains every client schema field exactly once, with the supplied schema's labels, order, required status, and field types preserved.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison with wintergate_preference_schema.xlsx.","grader_hint":"Normalize neither labels nor synonyms during comparison; compare the field inventory and order against the supplied schema."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every profile-entry cell is empty at delivery: it contains no text, number, copied source value, or formula.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell values in identified input cells.","grader_hint":"Use the schema and labels to identify entry cells and inspect cell.value, including formulas."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No named principal's personal preference or source-note value has been copied into the blank Profile instrument.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Profile values compared with cassilis_master_clienteling.xlsx.","grader_hint":"Search profile cells for source values and named-principal strings; labels and generic instructions are not personal values."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Mapping Key has one mapping row for every client schema field and no client field is omitted or duplicated.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mapping Key table contents.","grader_hint":"Compare the distinct Client field values to the schema inventory."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Mapping Key uses the exact client field labels and includes the required columns for required status, source field or note pattern, evidence rule, permitted normalization, unsupported treatment, and provenance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mapping Key headers and rows.","grader_hint":"Check header strings against the required mapping-key vocabulary and verify nonempty guidance for each row."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each mapping row distinguishes an explicit source statement from an inferred value and directs unsupported information to a blank or confirmation path.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mapping Key evidence and unsupported-treatment columns.","grader_hint":"Review every row against northgale_data_handling_note.docx; a generic instruction repeated for all fields is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The mapping rules correctly identify the legitimate source relationship for each field that is explicitly supported by the master sheet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mapping Key compared with source workbook.","grader_hint":"For each supported field, verify that the named source column or note pattern actually contains the relevant information."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Dietary escalation contact is present in the schema mapping and is explicitly marked blank pending supported confirmation when the master source lacks it.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dietary escalation contact row.","grader_hint":"Require both field presence and an unsupported/confirmation instruction; do not award for merely mentioning the phrase."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Allergy severity tier is mapped without inventing a severity from an allergy mention and is explicitly routed to confirmation when severity evidence is absent.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Allergy severity tier row and handling guidance.","grader_hint":"Reject rules that convert any allergy note into a severity tier without explicit supporting evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Standing car preference is present and the mapping distinguishes an explicit standing preference from a one-off transport note.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Standing car preference row.","grader_hint":"Check that the rule does not promote incidental transportation information into a standing preference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Controlled profile fields have data-validation rules whose allowed values exactly match the corresponding client schema lists.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet dataValidations and schema workbook.","grader_hint":"Inspect validation formulas and resolved list values; compare each controlled field's set without allowing extra synonyms."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Validation rules apply to the full intended entry range rather than only the first visible record or a single example cell.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Validation sqref ranges.","grader_hint":"Confirm all relevant profile entry cells are covered and no rule depends on a source row count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"At least one completion or required-field status cell is formula-driven rather than a pasted constant.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Formula cells in Profile.","grader_hint":"Inspect formulas with data_only=False and reject literal status values."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The completion formula counts valid nonblank required entries and does not treat labels, formatting, or placeholders as completed answers.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Completion formula and schema required flags.","grader_hint":"Evaluate formula logic against an empty profile and test cells with valid, invalid, and placeholder-like text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains conditional formatting that visibly identifies required profile fields still lacking an entry.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conditional formatting rules and target ranges.","grader_hint":"Inspect rules and ranges; a static fill applied regardless of cell state does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook uses defined names or equivalent expansion-safe references for controlled lists or shared schema ranges.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Defined names and validation formulas.","grader_hint":"Inspect workbook.defined_names and ensure references are valid and not merely single hard-coded cells."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Adding a new schema-consistent source row or principal does not require changing fixed-row formulas, validation definitions, or the mapping-key range.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Expansion test on a copy of the workbook.","grader_hint":"Append a synthetic row within the designed input structure and verify formulas and controls continue to cover it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The profile entry area is represented by an Excel Table or another structurally expandable object rather than a fixed range tied to today's source count.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Table definitions or equivalent range metadata.","grader_hint":"Inspect table.ref and formulas; reject fixed references that terminate at the supplied source row count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Instructions area explains how to identify entry cells, use controlled choices, interpret required-field highlighting, and read the completion indicator.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Instructions sheet text.","grader_hint":"Check for operational guidance covering all four actions, not just a title or general note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The instructions explicitly state that a blank value is not the same as no preference and explain how unsupported information is escalated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Instructions sheet text.","grader_hint":"Require both the semantic distinction and a follow-up/confirmation action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook preserves a usable provenance mechanism for recording the source or evidence behind a populated profile value.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Profile provenance affordance and mapping-key provenance guidance.","grader_hint":"Verify that provenance can be recorded per field or through an equally specific mechanism; a single unrelated note box is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Profile print settings are A4 portrait, fit to one page wide, and do not clip the schema labels or entry areas.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet page setup and rendered PDF.","grader_hint":"Inspect paper size, orientation, fitToWidth, and render the sheet to verify visible clipping does not occur."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Mapping Key print settings are A4 landscape, fit to one page wide, and repeat its header row when it spans multiple pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mapping Key page setup and print titles.","grader_hint":"Inspect pageSetup and print_title_rows; render to confirm columns remain usable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered Profile sheet is no more than one page wide and has no clipped columns, hidden required labels, or truncated controlled-value guidance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook pages.","grader_hint":"Use PDF rendering or an equivalent office renderer and inspect the complete horizontal extent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook has frozen panes or an equivalent navigation aid that keeps the useful profile or mapping headers visible during scrolling.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet freeze panes.","grader_hint":"Inspect freeze_panes on Profile and Mapping Key and confirm the frozen area contains relevant headers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Visual formatting distinguishes editable entry cells, calculated status, and instructional or mapping content without altering blank-cell semantics.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Styles, fills, protection state, and cell contents.","grader_hint":"Inspect style patterns and confirm formatting is informative while profile inputs remain empty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains no macros, external links, passwords, logos, or invented client data.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"OOXML relationships, workbook properties, drawings, and cell values.","grader_hint":"Inspect package relationships and drawings, then search values for unsupported personal records or sample answers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A new concierge can use the blank workbook correctly without verbal training: the schema is easy to scan, controlled choices are apparent, deliberate blanks are understandable, and the mapping key supports a defensible handoff to Ingrid.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and end-to-end reviewer walkthrough.","grader_hint":"Have an independent reviewer perform a short blank-profile walkthrough using only the workbook and supplied references; score down for ambiguity, crowded presentation, unexplained status signals, or guidance that invites guessing."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Nnamdi Falkenrath is preparing a reusable client-intake workbook for Cassilis House Management's concierge team. The workbook will be used by staff who convert shorthand principal notes into a client-mandated preference profile before review by Ingrid Solheim.","difficulty_sources":["The client schema contains fields that are absent from the shorthand master sheet, so the preparer must distinguish legitimate mappings from unsupported inference.","The workbook must remain usable as the number of principals and source rows grows without embedding today's row count in formulas or validation ranges.","The intake form must be clear enough for a concierge to complete while retaining the exact vocabulary, provenance, and blank-field discipline required by the principal-services director."],"authoring_plan":{"polarity":"blank","source_design":{"cassilis_master_clienteling.xlsx":"Create a clean but shorthand source table with named-principal records, explicit preferences, note fragments, and several absent client-schema concepts. Include legitimate mappings for ordinary preferences, at least one safely normalizable note, and unsupported gaps for dietary escalation contact, allergy severity tier, and standing car preference. Keep source records mutually consistent and synthetic.","wintergate_preference_schema.xlsx":"Define the exact client schema, including field labels, field types, required/optional status, controlled lists, and review order. Include fields whose names or concepts do not appear in the master source. Use stable arbitrary vocabulary that the solver can read from this file.","northgale_data_handling_note.docx":"Define explicit evidence versus inference, permitted normalization, provenance expectations, follow-up treatment, and the rule that unsupported sensitive details remain blank. Provide enough operational guidance to justify mapping choices without dictating a cell layout.","principal_services_review_brief.docx":"State that the workbook is completed electronically, reviewed by Ingrid, sometimes printed on A4, and used by a new concierge. Require a visible completion signal, controlled entry choices, a separate mapping reference, and expansion-safe construction."},"workbook_structure":{"sheets":["Profile","Mapping Key","Instructions"],"profile":{"purpose":"Blank single-principal instrument.","schema_source":"Replicate every schema field exactly from wintergate_preference_schema.xlsx, preserving field labels, required markers, field types, controlled vocabulary, and order.","entry_cells":"Each client field has a dedicated empty entry cell. No principal values or examples are placed in these cells.","affordances":["A formula-driven completion indicator counts only valid, nonblank required entries and distinguishes unresolved blanks.","Controlled fields use validation lists derived from the schema rather than hard-coded one-off cells.","Required-but-empty cells receive conditional formatting; formatting must not insert values.","A principal identifier and review metadata area is present but contains no sample data.","Use an Excel Table or expansion-safe ranges for profile structure where applicable; formulas must not rely on today's source row count."]},"mapping_key":{"purpose":"Operational source-mapping control for every schema field.","required_columns":["Client field","Required status","Source field or note pattern","Evidence rule","Permitted normalization","If unsupported or absent","Provenance to retain"],"content":"One row per client schema field, using exact client labels. Explicitly mark fields that must remain blank pending confirmation. Do not place principal-specific values in the key.","growth":"Build the key as a structured table or equivalent expansion-safe range and keep any lookup or validation references robust to added rows."},"instructions":{"purpose":"Explain the blank instrument to an untrained concierge.","content":["How to identify entry cells and controlled choices","How to read the completion indicator and required-field highlighting","How to use the mapping key and record provenance","How to handle unsupported information and escalation","A clear statement that blank is not the same as no preference"]},"print_and_usability":{"profile":"A4 portrait, one page wide, with readable labels and no clipped entry areas.","mapping_key":"A4 landscape, one page wide, with repeated header row and legible columns.","instructions":"Readable as a separate reference page.","navigation":"Freeze the useful header area, use clear tab names, and preserve visual distinction between input, guidance, and calculated status.","tradeoff":"Allow wrapping and adequate row height for long mapping guidance while keeping the profile scan-friendly; numerical completion logic must remain accurate despite the visual treatment."}},"gold_derivation":"Build a reference workbook with the above structure, then reopen it with openpyxl in formula-preserving and data-only modes, inspect defined names, validations, conditional formatting, tables, formulas, and print properties, and render sheets to PDF for page-count and clipping review. Verify that all profile entry cells are empty and that adding a synthetic row or schema-consistent record does not require rewriting fixed-row formulas or validation references."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"master_clienteling_source","filename":"cassilis_master_clienteling.xlsx","purpose":"The current shorthand master clienteling workbook. It contains complete, internally consistent source notes and field values for the named principals and is the source material from which legitimate mappings must be identified.","required":true,"discovery":"Open this workbook first to identify the source columns, note conventions, and explicit versus absent information; do not treat an absent field as a value."},{"artifact_id":"client_schema","filename":"wintergate_preference_schema.xlsx","purpose":"Wintergate Engineering's mandated principal preference schema, including exact field labels, required status, controlled vocabularies, field order, and client-facing terminology.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this workbook as the controlling specification for the profile fields and permitted values."},{"artifact_id":"handling_guidance","filename":"northgale_data_handling_note.docx","purpose":"Operational guidance defining explicit evidence, safe normalization, follow-up status, unsupported inference, and escalation treatment for sensitive or absent preference information.","required":true,"discovery":"Read this document when deciding whether a shorthand note can populate a field, needs normalization, or must remain blank."},{"artifact_id":"review_brief","filename":"principal_services_review_brief.docx","purpose":"The principal-services director's review and print requirements, including how the blank template, completion indication, mapping key, and unresolved items will be used.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this brief to set the workbook's review usability and print behaviour."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"profile_workbook","filename":"principal_preference_profile.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A blank per-principal preference profile workbook containing the exact Wintergate schema and a source-mapping key.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.","Keep every profile-entry cell empty at delivery; do not include examples, copied principal values, guessed values, or placeholder answers.","Use the exact field labels, controlled values, escalation terms, and required indicators from the supplied schema and handling guidance.","Make formulas, named ranges, validations, conditional formatting, and print settings continue to function when source data grows beyond the supplied rows.","The mapping key must document source evidence, permitted normalization, provenance expectations, and deliberate-blank or follow-up treatment for every client field.","The workbook must open without repair warnings and must not contain macros, external links, logos, or passwords."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"form_or_template","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"artifact_spec@v4","occupation":"concierges","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"artifact_spec","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Build the reference workbook from the supplied synthetic sources, then have an independent spreadsheet reviewer inspect both object structure and rendered pages. The reviewer must verify blank-input discipline, schema fidelity, source-mapping defensibility, expansion behaviour, and practical use by an untrained concierge.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["Different spreadsheet renderers may paginate wrapped mapping guidance slightly differently, so print checks should focus on the specified paper size, width fit, repeated headers, and absence of clipping rather than a fixed total page count.","Formula recalculation may require a spreadsheet engine; structural formula presence and logical evaluation should be tested separately."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:16+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:16+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:16+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:16+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:16+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/4f9f8c3f852c1911","declared_deliverables":["principal_preference_profile.xlsx"]};
